From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucas gelfond <lucasgelfond@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/29] demux: ogg: let the decoders drain at the end of the file

At the end of a group of logical streams the demuxer deletes its
elementary streams and looks for a chained group. Deleting an ES kills its
decoder at once, so whatever had just been sent was never played: with a
skeleton track, or any group of more than one stream, a short file played
nothing and a long one lost its tail.

When nothing follows in the file, report the end of the stream and keep the
ES, so the decoders drain as for any other demuxer.
---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/demux/ogg.c b/modules/demux/ogg.c
--- a/modules/demux/ogg.c
+++ b/modules/demux/ogg.c
@@ -416,6 +416,18 @@ static int Demux( demux_t * p_demux )
 
             vlc_tick_t i_lastdts = Ogg_GetLastDTS( p_demux );
 
+            /* Nothing follows: keep the elementary streams. Deleting them
+             * kills their decoders before they have played what was just
+             * sent, which is all of a short file. */
+            const uint8_t *p_peek;
+            if( p_sys->oy.fill <= p_sys->oy.returned &&
+                vlc_stream_Peek( p_demux->s, &p_peek, 1 ) < 1 )
+            {
+                if( i_lastdts != VLC_TICK_INVALID && likely( !p_sys->b_slave ) )
+                    es_out_SetPCR( p_demux->out, i_lastdts );
+                return VLC_DEMUXER_EOF;
+            }
+
             /* We keep the ES to try reusing it in Ogg_BeginningOfStream
              * only 1 ES is supported (common case for ogg web radio) */
             if( p_sys->i_streams == 1 && p_sys->i_declared_streams == 1 && p_sys->pp_stream[0]->p_es )
